The two `warning: bevy_siren (example ...) generated 1 warning` lines are the same macOS linker message for a Bevy debug binary - `ld: __eh_frame section too large (max 16MB) to encode dwarf unwind offsets in compact unwind table` - that
`example "mixer"` has always had; `example "quick_start"` (a DefaultPlugins example) has it too. Clippy, which does not link, is clean under -D warnings.
